Hello,

<% if @first_year %>
  <% case @days_to_expire %>
  <% when 30 %>
    We're reaching out because your program expiration is coming up on <%= @expiration_date %>.

    Want to continue on GitHub Enterprise? We're offering startups associated with an <%= link_to("approved GitHub for Startups partner", "#{GitHub.help_url}/enterprise/startups/partners") %> a 50% discount on GitHub Enterprise for their second year in the program.

    GitHub for Startups Enterprise <%= link_to("features", "#{GitHub.help_url}/pricing/") %>:

    - 50K Action mins per month
    - User Management (SSO)
    - Organizational Controls (SOC)
    - …and exclusive events, office hours, and webinars!

    Interested in GitHub Advanced Security? We're also inviting startups returning to the program and new to Advanced security a 50% discount on GitHub Advanced Security!

    - <%= link_to("Code Scanning", DocsUrlConfig.url_for("code-security/about-code-scanning")) %> - Search for potential security vulnerabilities and coding errors.
    - <%= link_to("Secret Scanning", "https://docs.github.com/en/code-security/secret-scanning/about-secret-scanning") %> -  Detect secrets (keys, tokens, etc.) in private repos.
    - <%= link_to("Dependency Review", "https://docs.github.com/en/code-security/supply-chain-security/understanding-your-software-supply-chain/about-dependency-review") %> - Show the full impact of changes to dependencies and vulnerable versions before you merge a pull request.

    To ensure your Enterprise plan is not interrupted, please notify us with your intent to continue on GitHub Enterprise at least 5 business days before your program expiration.

    Otherwise, your organization will automatically be downgraded to a Free plan on your termination date, and your Enterprise Account will be deleted. You will be notified once your organization has been removed from the Enterprise, at which time you may self-serve upgrade to a Team plan if you wish.

    Thank you again for building with GitHub for Startups! Please let us know if you have any questions.
  <% when 3 %>
    We're following up as your access to GitHub for Startups expires in 3 days.

    Would you like to take advantage of the 50% discount for your second year in the program?

    If so, we kindly ask that you please confirm if you'd like to continue on GitHub Enterprise and the GitHub for Startups <%= link_to("partner", "#{GitHub.help_url}/enterprise/startups/partners") %> you're associated with so that we can send over a quote and next steps.

    If not, no worries. Once your termination is processed, you'll be notified when your organization(s) are removed from your Enterprise Account and downgraded to a Free plan. Once that takes place, you'll have the ability to remain on the free tier or self-serve purchase the Team plan. If you receive an invoice for any consumptive add-ons, you will still be able to pay in the admin dashboard.

    Thanks again for having been a part of GitHub for Startups!
  <% end %>
<% else %>
  <% case @days_to_expire %>
  <% when 30 %>
    Thank you for being a part of GitHub for Startups!

    We're reaching out as your program expiration date is coming up on <%= @expiration_date %>.

    At this time, we're offering you a GitHub for Startups graduation discount redeemable within 30 days of program graduation:

    - Evaluation + GitHub Enterprise - 20% discount
    - Evaluation + GitHub Enterprise + Advanced Security -  25% discount

    GitHub Advanced Security:

    - <%= link_to("Code Scanning", DocsUrlConfig.url_for("code-security/about-code-scanning")) %> - Search for potential security vulnerabilities and coding errors.
    - <%= link_to("Secret Scanning", "https://docs.github.com/en/code-security/secret-scanning/about-secret-scanning") %> -  Detect secrets (keys, tokens, etc.) in private repos.
    - <%= link_to("Dependency Review", "https://docs.github.com/en/code-security/supply-chain-security/understanding-your-software-supply-chain/about-dependency-review") %> - Show the full impact of changes to dependencies and vulnerable versions before you merge a pull request.

    If you're interested in the above, please respond to this email at your earliest convenience.

    If we don't hear from you, your organization will automatically be downgraded to a Free plan on your termination date, and your Enterprise Account will be deleted. You will be notified once your organization has been removed from the Enterprise, at which time you may self-serve upgrade to the Team tier if you wish.

    Thank you again for building with GitHub for Startups! Please let us know if you have any questions.
  <% when 3 %>
    We're following up as your access to GitHub Enterprise expires in 3 days.

    At this time, we're offering you a GitHub for Startups graduation discount redeemable within 30 days of program graduation:

    - Evaluation + GitHub Enterprise - 20% discount
    - Evaluation + GitHub Enterprise + Advanced Security - 25% discount

    If you're interested in the above, please respond to this email ASAP.

    If not, no worries. Once your termination is processed, you'll be notified when your organization(s) are removed from your Enterprise Account and downgraded to a Free plan. Once that takes place, you'll have the ability to remain on the free tier or self-serve purchase the Team plan. If you receive an invoice for any consumptive add-ons, you will still be able to pay in the admin dashboard.

    Thanks again for having been a part of GitHub for Startups!
  <% end %>
<% end %>

The GitHub for Startup Team

